        car.start();
    }
}
```

In this modified code, we have two interfaces `Vehicle` and `Machine`, both containing a default implementation of the `start()` method. The `Car` class implements both interfaces and overrides the `start()` method to resolve the diamond inheritance problem. By calling `Vehicle.super.start()` and `Machine.super.start()`, we can explicitly choose which implementation to use.

